\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Dynamics calculated using the Lindblad equation reflect damping and dissipation.
 (a) The QHO modeled using the quantum Liouville equation behaves as a closed-system,
 in which oscillations persist forever.
 In the case of Lindblad evolution,
 however,
 damping is evident as oscillations decrease in amplitude with time.
 (b) In the energy basis,
 Liouvillian evolution conserves energy,
 but an exponential decrease in energy is evident in the open system modeled using the Lindblad equation.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "fig:qho-dynamics-coherent-vs-lindblad"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Lindblad Operators for the Quantum Harmonic Oscillator - Thermalization
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Another option for the QHO is to use a pair of Lindblad operators,
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\left\{ \hat{L}_{1},\hat{L}_{2}\right\} =\left\{ \frac{1}{\sqrt{T_{1}}}\hat{a},\frac{1}{\sqrt{T_{1}}}e^{-\frac{\hbar\omega}{k_{B}T}}\hat{a}^{\dagger}\right\} 
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Here,
 the second Lindblad operator is proportional to the raising operator,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{a}^{\dagger}$
\end_inset

,
 so we should expect it to excite the system (adding energy)
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
The second Lindblad operator,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{L}_{2}$
\end_inset

,
 has an additional (small) weight of 
\begin_inset Formula $e^{-\frac{\hbar\omega}{2k_{B}T}}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
This maintains relaxation via 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{L}_{1}$
\end_inset

 as the dominant effect,
 but models the fact that the system can be excited by thermal energy in the environment at temperature 
\begin_inset Formula $T$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
In the limit of 
\begin_inset Formula $T\rightarrow0$
\end_inset

,
 the operator 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{L}_{2}\rightarrow0$
\end_inset

,
 so that we have relaxation,
 as in the previous case
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
The code below calculates the time evolution of a QHO under thermalization,
 and results are shown in Figures 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:qho-dynamics-2-1"

\end_inset

 (position basis) and 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:qho-dynamics-3-1"

\end_inset

 (energy basis)
\end_layout

